{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical","id":1525827,"title":"Why is WoD so cynical?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-23T02:22:54-08:00","id":1525827,"title":"Why is WoD so cynical?","content":"I've read some of the WoD 20th anniversary book, about Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, and I got to say that it's much more cynical than I expected, I thought WoD was more absurd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T05:44:41-08:00","id":1525838,"title":"","content":"It always drew fairly heavily from certain parts of Film Noir, Cyberpunk, and 1970s cinema in addition to classic Gothic fiction and the various game specific influences (Anne Rice, Wolfen, 1984, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T05:47:40-08:00","id":1525839,"title":"","content":"It's both, and for many the juxtaposition between the absurdity and playing it straight makes for much of the appeal. It's an 80s/90s Zeitgeist thing that still shows through in the 20th Anniversary edition, but has shifted slightly over time with how overt it is. While I wouldn't exactly call WoD a grimdark setting, it shares many elements with that genre. If you look at something like Warhammer 40.000 - the genre codifier - you have completely overt absurd stuff like spaceships that are literal cathedrals, complete with gothic architecture, but everybody in-universe treats it as straight up normal.<br /> WoD is like that, but subtler. Young Gen Xers were deeply cynical, trying to alleviate a very bleak looking future with joking about how absurd their situation seemed, and that translated into the media of the time. If you can't change it, you can at least try and laugh about it. That aspect of the WoD decreased over time, but never completely vanished. Basically you are given the option to emphasize either cynic or absurdist elements as you like, depending on what kind of game you want to run. Both work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T07:33:18-08:00","id":1525841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical#post1525827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read some of the WoD 20th anniversary book, about Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, and I got to say that it's much more cynical than I expected, I thought WoD was more absurd?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is some disconnect between how WoD books presented things, the setting material, different play styles, and the stories of games that tend to be shared.<br /> <br /> 1st Edition of the games had absurd elements, but generally pushed a very street level punk play style (early on at least), 2nd Edition tended to expand the settings in ways that pulled away from street level play, then Revised tried to (for better and worse) pull back towards street level and occasionally make changes to the setting to enforce that. This led to a pretty big spread of play styles, and I think the more absurd ones tended to be the stories that got shared.<br /> <br /> I don't think the books were <i>usually</i> that absurd, but people often did pretty absurd things with them. I'm pretty sure I played in a group where a ST had a character who had been a vampire, turned human, became a mage or something, then a Kami? It was very stupid, but those tend to be the stories that get shared. I've played a lot of VtM and there were never vampires in trench coats with katanas and shotguns loaded with dragonsbreath rounds, but it was such a trope that I'm pretty sure there was a sidebar in one of the Revised books about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T09:29:14-08:00","id":1525846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical#post1525827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read some of the WoD 20th anniversary book, about Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, and I got to say that it's much more cynical than I expected, I thought WoD was more absurd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because WoD is mostly a Gen X creation, and that's the cynicism of that generation.<br /> <br /> As a millennial thou, I'm happy that it was Gen X and not made by millennials, otherwise it would be some sugar and rainbows and unicorns and how the power of love saves everything blergh \ud83e\udd22","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:04:36-08:00","id":1525851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1525846#post1525846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because WoD is mostly a Gen X creation, and that's the cynicism of that generation.<br /> <br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>As a member of Gen X, I say, what cynicism? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:38:02-08:00","id":1525856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1525851#post1525851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a member of Gen X, I say, what cynicism?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think my favorite take on that was from MTV's Daria, where her mom asked if she was depressed and her best friend said, &quot;no, just realistic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/