in one of the Revised books about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was in the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T18:42:01-08:00","id":1526028,"title":"","content":"It's right there on the tin. Setting not called World of Hugs and Puppies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T08:42:21-08:00","id":1526068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526028#post1526028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's right there on the tin. Setting not called World of Hugs and Puppies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darkness is something that's interpreted massively different ways between different people. This is particularly true in the case of different games, some of which have no time for the way that the other game works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T00:25:21-08:00","id":1526505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a millennial thou, I'm happy that it was Gen X and not made by millennials, otherwise it would be some sugar and rainbows and unicorns and how the power of love saves everything blergh \ud83e\udd22</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that our prevailing stereotype? I'm an older millennial myself and I'm probably more cynical than most Gen Xers I've met.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T10:01:43-08:00","id":1526518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526505#post1526505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that our prevailing stereotype? I'm an older millennial myself and I'm probably more cynical than most Gen Xers I've met.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a cynic too, as you probably could tell, but it seems we are the outliners of our generation. Or maybe we are already getting too old to be young, and we are getting a little grumpy \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T12:59:58-08:00","id":1526565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526505#post1526505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that our prevailing stereotype? I'm an older millennial myself and I'm probably more cynical than most Gen Xers I've met.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just thought out about the perfect example that encapsulates the average millennial mindset. 2 examples actually.<br /> <br /> The first is Harry Potter, that wins not because he is the best or most skilled, but because of his friends and because he is &quot;special&quot;. Blergh \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd2e<br /> <br /> The second is Peter Quill, in Guardians of the Galaxy 1. In the end, he defeats Ronan the Accuser because... He is special... Oh yes, and also by the power of holding hands. Blergh \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd2e<br /> <br /> So, we are definitely the outliners amongst our generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T17:12:48-08:00","id":1526575,"title":"","content":"Most of my friends are depressed queers, I'm still not so sure about your examples.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T18:12:03-08:00","id":1526577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1525846#post1525846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because WoD is mostly a Gen X creation, and that's the cynicism of that generation.<br /> <br /> As a millennial thou, I'm happy that it was Gen X and not made by millennials, otherwise it would be some sugar and rainbows and unicorns and how the power of love saves everything blergh \ud83e\udd22</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with optimism, sugar and rainbows and unicorns definitely have their place, but that place is not VtM. That being said, even cynical vampires can benefit from the power of friendship, maybe all the more so because they\u2019re so cynical normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T19:54:46-08:00","id":1526578,"title":"","content":"Being a Gen Xer as well as a lawyer, I think I have my share of cynicism about the state of the world, but more than a few things give me hope for the future despite me being scared shitless by climate change and the new rise of fascism around the world and here at home. Rather than turn this into a political discussion, I'll just leave it at that.<br /> <br /> As for absurdity being played up in some troupes' WoD games, I was involved in this one Mage campaign where the ST was nice enough to let me play a Bubasti since I didn't feel near confident or competent enough to play Mage's magick rules. Two of the other PCs were an Orphan and an alcoholic Hermetic. And the last player's character was a defecting Void Engineer. A motley crew if ever there was one.<br /> <br /> At the start of the campaign, my Bubasti character was told to rendezvous with this VE inside the stairwell of a high-rise building (don't ask why there, I don't remember the details). So this VE botches his Correspondence roll when he teleports to the stairwell and winds up rolling down at least three floors of stairs only to land in a heap in front of my Bubasti (who has his pistol drawn because of all the noise). The relationship between the two PCs only went downhill from there. :-P<br /> <br /> Later on, the VE and my Bubasti were forced to share a two-bed hotel room. Because the two of them didn't get along <i>at all</i>, my Bubasti decide to wait until the VE was asleep in his bed, then shifted into Feline form and urinated on him. With my superb Stealth roll, I was able to pull it off <i>without waking him up</i>. It was <i>way </i>better than finding a horse's head in your bed! :-D<br /> <br /> As for the reason a Bubasti was running with a mage troupe? The justification for having a Bubasti run with these mages was that the kheper (the Bubasti tribe elders) were trying to establish goodwill relations with mages to find new allies in their war against the Followers of Set. My PC was chosen to be the first attempt at this ambassadorial role. Needless to say, it...did not go as planned. :-P<br /> <br /> Oh, and that VE player? He's been my best friend in RL ever since. :-D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T01:20:31-08:00","id":1526585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526578#post1526578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Gen Xer as well as a lawyer, I think I have my share of cynicism about the state of the world, but more than a few things give me hope for the future despite me being scared shitless by climate change and the new rise of fascism around the world and here at home. Rather than turn this into a political discussion, I'll just leave it at that.<br /> <br /> As for absurdity being played up in some troupes' WoD games, I was involved in this one Mage campaign where the ST was nice enough to let me play a Bubasti since I didn't feel near confident or competent enough to play Mage's magick rules. Two of the other PCs were an Orphan and an alcoholic Hermetic. And the last player's character was a defecting Void Engineer. A motley crew if ever there was one.<br /> <br /> At the start of the campaign, my Bubasti character was told to rendezvous with this VE inside the stairwell of a high-rise building (don't ask why there, I don't remember the details). So this VE botches his Correspondence roll when he teleports to the stairwell and winds up rolling down at least three floors of stairs only to land in a heap in front of my Bubasti (who has his pistol drawn because of all the noise). The relationship between the two PCs only went downhill from there. :-P<br /> <br /> Later on, the VE and my Bubasti were forced to share a two-bed hotel room. Because the two of them didn't get along <i>at all</i>, my Bubasti decide to wait until the VE was asleep in his bed, then shifted into Feline form and urinated on him. With my superb Stealth roll, I was able to pull it off <i>without waking him up</i>. It was <i>way </i>better than finding a horse's head in your bed! :-D<br /> <br /> As for the reason a Bubasti was running with a mage troupe? The justification for having a Bubasti run with these mages was that the kheper (the Bubasti tribe elders) were trying to establish goodwill relations with mages to find new allies in their war against the Followers of Set. My PC was chosen to be the first attempt at this ambassadorial role. Needless to say, it...did not go as planned. :-P<br /> <br /> Oh, and that VE player? He's been my best friend in RL ever since. :-D</div> </div> </div> </div>That is so awesome! About your best friend. And I\u2019m a lawyer too. I\u2019m also basically an optimistic person despite enjoying games like World of Darkness and Kult back in college and law school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T01:22:07-08:00","id":1526586,"title":"","content":"Well, I never actually played Kult, but I really liked the idea in spite of its intense nihilism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T03:52:58-08:00","id":1526589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526577#post1526577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing wrong with optimism, sugar and rainbows and unicorns definitely have their place, but that place is not VtM. That being said, even cynical vampires can benefit from the power of friendship, maybe all the more so because they\u2019re so cynical normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Optimism sugar rainbows and unicorns are wonderful for the real life, in so far as you're not dumb enough to forget that the world is a harsh world filled with evil. But yes, having a positive attitude towards life is wonderful.<br /> <br /> However, rainbows and sugar and hippies and shine happy people holding hands is definitely NOT something that I enjoy in artistic expressions. Personal taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T04:49:31-08:00","id":1526590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526589#post1526589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Optimism sugar rainbows and unicorns are wonderful for the real life, in so far as you're not dumb enough to forget that the world is a harsh world filled with evil. But yes, having a positive attitude towards life is wonderful.<br /> <br /> However, rainbows and sugar and hippies and shine happy people holding hands is definitely NOT something that I enjoy in artistic expressions. Personal taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Not everyone is into sugary sweet happiness in art. I personally prefer optimism, which is I guess why lately I prefer D&amp;D to the World of Darkness (the main reason I like WoD is because I like vampires and also the urban fantasy of Mage and Changeling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T05:43:16-08:00","id":1526592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526590#post1526590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand. Not everyone is into sugary sweet happiness in art. I personally prefer optimism, which is I guess why lately I prefer D&amp;D to the World of Darkness (the main reason I like WoD is because I like vampires and also the urban fantasy of Mage and Changeling).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like D&amp;D and I like the fact that you're undeniably the hero (most of the time), instead of the WoD &quot;50 shades of asshole&quot;. Indeed, it gets tiresome after a while. But in D&amp;D you don't just simply win the day all the time by the power of holding hands... I don't know if you get my meaning. Lord of the Rings is my favorite story of all times, and it is absolutely positive in every way, but it is not sugarcoated super boring sunshines. I utterly despise the utterly nihilistic and absolutely void of any meaning Game of Thrones (A Song of Ice and Fire), as the nihilistic garbage made by a wealthy hippie boomer. So it's not about being optimistic or pessimistic, but about doing it properly. WoD is over the top and it's satirical, which is why it is so fun.<br /> <br /> Peter Quill from Guardians of the Galaxy is a quintessential Millennial. A rebel without a cause, but despite that still have a good heart and wanna do good, just without following social conventions to do so. And he also works well with others, because Millennials, despite being spoiled little brats, are very social and agreeable. He is also SPECIAL - let's not forget, he is the Scion of a god (with a low case &quot;g&quot; when his daddy is feeling humble).<br /> <br /> The part of being &quot;special&quot; and winning the day by the power of holding hands is what I have a problem with. Likewise, Harry Potter wins the day not because he's smarter or stronger or more skilled or because he has greater moral fiber or stronger will, but because he's special... Again, another Millennial &quot;trait&quot; that makes me puck inside.<br /> <br /> As a comparison, in Lord of the Rings, the heroes win because they acquired the skills to do so, because they are willing to self sacrifice for others and because of their moral strength. Frodo goes to Mount Doom because he knew it was the right thing to do; Sam helps him out of duty to his best friend. Aragorn spent decades as a Ranger to acquire all of the skills that he uses on behalf of his people. Except for Aragorn, none of them are particularly special, and even for Aragorn - or Boromir or even Legolas - even thou they are &quot;special&quot; due to their social statuses (they are basically aristocrats), their higher status is NOT a reason for merely living in luxury, but instead they have a duty to their people. Boromir leads Gondor as their captain, fighting in the front lines and commanding his men in front of them, as does Aragorn, Faramir or Legolas and Gimli. So, Aragorn is &quot;Special&quot; (he's destined to become the King), but this represents a duty for him, and he still had to prepare for decades to be able to lead his people.<br /> <br /> It's vastly different from the Millennial &quot;literature&quot; upon which you are special simply from birth, because you're &quot;mom and daddy little spoiled brat&quot;","signature":""