uintessential Millennial. A rebel without a cause, but despite that still have a good heart and wanna do good, just without following social conventions to do so. And he also works well with others, because Millennials, despite being spoiled little brats, are very social and agreeable. He is also SPECIAL - let's not forget, he is the Scion of a god (with a low case &quot;g&quot; when his daddy is feeling humble).<br /> <br /> The part of being &quot;special&quot; and winning the day by the power of holding hands is what I have a problem with. Likewise, Harry Potter wins the day not because he's smarter or stronger or more skilled or because he has greater moral fiber or stronger will, but because he's special... Again, another Millennial &quot;trait&quot; that makes me puck inside.<br /> <br /> As a comparison, in Lord of the Rings, the heroes win because they acquired the skills to do so, because they are willing to self sacrifice for others and because of their moral strength. Frodo goes to Mount Doom because he knew it was the right thing to do; Sam helps him out of duty to his best friend. Aragorn spent decades as a Ranger to acquire all of the skills that he uses on behalf of his people. Except for Aragorn, none of them are particularly special, and even for Aragorn - or Boromir or even Legolas - even thou they are &quot;special&quot; due to their social statuses (they are basically aristocrats), their higher status is NOT a reason for merely living in luxury, but instead they have a duty to their people. Boromir leads Gondor as their captain, fighting in the front lines and commanding his men in front of them, as does Aragorn, Faramir or Legolas and Gimli. So, Aragorn is &quot;Special&quot; (he's destined to become the King), but this represents a duty for him, and he still had to prepare for decades to be able to lead his people.<br /> <br /> It's vastly different from the Millennial &quot;literature&quot; upon which you are special simply from birth, because you're &quot;mom and daddy little spoiled brat&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you\u2019re saying. I disagree with your basic premise that winning by the power of holding hands is inherently a bad thing, but I agree with some of your points about D&amp;D and Lord of the Rings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-16-2023, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T17:31:36-08:00","id":1526641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526592#post1526592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like D&amp;D and I like the fact that you're undeniably the hero (most of the time), instead of the WoD &quot;50 shades of asshole&quot;. Indeed, it gets tiresome after a while. But in D&amp;D you don't just simply win the day all the time by the power of holding hands... I don't know if you get my meaning. Lord of the Rings is my favorite story of all times, and it is absolutely positive in every way, but it is not sugarcoated super boring sunshines. I utterly despise the utterly nihilistic and absolutely void of any meaning Game of Thrones (A Song of Ice and Fire), as the nihilistic garbage made by a wealthy hippie boomer. So it's not about being optimistic or pessimistic, but about doing it properly. WoD is over the top and it's satirical, which is why it is so fun.<br /> <br /> Peter Quill from Guardians of the Galaxy is a quintessential Millennial. A rebel without a cause, but despite that still have a good heart and wanna do good, just without following social conventions to do so. And he also works well with others, because Millennials, despite being spoiled little brats, are very social and agreeable. He is also SPECIAL - let's not forget, he is the Scion of a god (with a low case &quot;g&quot; when his daddy is feeling humble).<br /> <br /> The part of being &quot;special&quot; and winning the day by the power of holding hands is what I have a problem with. Likewise, Harry Potter wins the day not because he's smarter or stronger or more skilled or because he has greater moral fiber or stronger will, but because he's special... Again, another Millennial &quot;trait&quot; that makes me puck inside.<br /> <br /> As a comparison, in Lord of the Rings, the heroes win because they acquired the skills to do so, because they are willing to self sacrifice for others and because of their moral strength. Frodo goes to Mount Doom because he knew it was the right thing to do; Sam helps him out of duty to his best friend. Aragorn spent decades as a Ranger to acquire all of the skills that he uses on behalf of his people. Except for Aragorn, none of them are particularly special, and even for Aragorn - or Boromir or even Legolas - even thou they are &quot;special&quot; due to their social statuses (they are basically aristocrats), their higher status is NOT a reason for merely living in luxury, but instead they have a duty to their people. Boromir leads Gondor as their captain, fighting in the front lines and commanding his men in front of them, as does Aragorn, Faramir or Legolas and Gimli. So, Aragorn is &quot;Special&quot; (he's destined to become the King), but this represents a duty for him, and he still had to prepare for decades to be able to lead his people.<br /> <br /> It's vastly different from the Millennial &quot;literature&quot; upon which you are special simply from birth, because you're &quot;mom and daddy little spoiled brat&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I just don't see it. One, Harry Potter isn't even written by a millennial. J.K. Rowling is a Gen Xer herself. Not to mention a horrible, horrible person, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Star Lord? Ehhh... I mean, can anyone look at the screenwriter's age? I know that the director most definitely isn't a millennial either.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, both of your examples are white heteronormative males, which are kinda going out of fashion with our generation. Like I said, most of my friends are depressed queers and none of them are particularly enthusiastic about these characters you list.<br /> <br /> Maybe the hugbox part of millennial is straight, I dunno, but my community has consistently been prone to gallows humor in the circles I frequent.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the stereotype you're painting.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T09:39:13-08:00","id":1526682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526641#post1526641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I just don't see it. One, Harry Potter isn't even written by a millennial. J.K. Rowling is a Gen Xer herself. Not to mention a horrible, horrible person, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Star Lord? Ehhh... I mean, can anyone look at the screenwriter's age? I know that the director most definitely isn't a millennial either.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, both of your examples are white heteronormative males, which are kinda going out of fashion with our generation. Like I said, most of my friends are depressed queers and none of them are particularly enthusiastic about these characters you list.<br /> <br /> Maybe the hugbox part of millennial is straight, I dunno, but my community has consistently been prone to gallows humor in the circles I frequent.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the stereotype you're painting.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah well, those may be Gen X writers, but they weren't writing for the smallest generation ever (at the time), they were writing for the Millennials. That was the target audience.<br /> <br /> Now, your social circle may be made of exclusively by &quot;depressed queers&quot; as you put it, but I assure you that this demographic represents a minority of the overall population. And people aren't robots fabricated in series. I from my part have met several happy and positive queers of my generation.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;white heteronormative males&quot;, as a &quot;white heteronormative male&quot; myself I don't particularly enjoy having my own traits - to which I have absolutely no fault of my own to possess, after all I didn't choose to be born with them - being so lightly throw away in such a derogatory fashion. I'm sure you don't like that kind of experience either so. There's no need to despise people based on their colour of skin, gender or sexual orientation, don't you agree? (Besides, J.K.R is not a male last time I checked)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T10:26:27-08:00","id":1526683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526592#post1526592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Peter Quill from Guardians of the Galaxy is a quintessential Millennial.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What. This makes absolutely no sense. Peter Quill is a monument to the '80s if ever there was one. All the music he listens to are pop tunes made in the '70s and are stored on a <i>Walkman</i> of all things. Not to mention he's constantly making pop culture references to '80s movies like Footloose. Considering that he hasn't been back to Earth since 1988 when he was eight years old, none of this is surprising.<br /> <br /> Thinking that Peter Quill somehow embodies millennials just because he's immature makes <i>no </i>sense. There are lots of people who are immature at <i>any </i>age, not just people born in recent years. Peter Quill doesn't represent the (supposed) immaturity of millennials, he's a Gen Xer <i>who stopped growing up at 8 years old</i>. I think TvTropes said it best: &quot;Peter Quill's entire schtick is trying <i>way</i> too hard to embody a <i>grade-schooler's</i> idea of a badass space hero.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> There's just so much more to unpack here, but I'm just gonna leave this at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 12-11-2023, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T05:33:53-08:00","id":1526700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526683#post1526683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What. This makes absolutely no sense. Peter Quill is a monument to the '80s if ever there was one. All the music he listens to are pop tunes made in the '70s and are stored on a <i>Walkman</i> of all things. Not to mention he's constantly making pop culture references to '80s movies like Footloose. Considering that he hasn't been back to Earth since 1988 when he was eight years old, none of this is surprising.<br /> <br /> Thinking that Peter Quill somehow embodies millennials just because he's immature makes <i>no </i>sense. There are lots of people who are immature at <i>any </i>age, not just people born in recent years. Peter Quill doesn't represent the (supposed) immaturity of millennials, he's a Gen Xer <i>who stopped growing up at 8 years old</i>. I think TvTropes said it best: &quot;Peter Quill's entire schtick is trying <i>way</i> too hard to embody a <i>grade-schooler's</i> idea of a badass space hero.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> There's just so much more to unpack here, but I'm just gonna leave this at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not due to him being immature. He may have a 80's cultural taste, but he behaves like a Millennial, not like a Gen X. Gen X are individualists. A Gen X media is like Highlander, where &quot;there can only be one&quot;. Millennials, despite the stereotype of being spoiled and immature (which sometimes is true but not always), are actually good at cooperating and working with others, and are usually optimistic. That's basically all that Guardians of the Galaxy is about, they learn to work together and to &quot;make the world (or galaxy in this case) a better place&quot;. Those are typical Millennial traits.<br /> <br /> He does have one Gen X trait thou, which is his nomadim. Gen Xers are more prone than others to not set roots in one place.<br /> <br /> Take in contrast for instance Back to the Future, where the protagonist is just a nobody common boy, who wins the day by being outright smarter than his opponents, and every mistakes he makes dooms the world to a utterly over the top cynical dystopian alternative future. So, he has to be THE BEST otherwise he's screwed. That's a very Gen X view of the world, as opposed to being the special &quot;Starlord&quot; who later on finds out to be a demigod. The rest of the Guardians are all special too mind you. They are all unique unicorns. Groot and the Raccoon are unique in the Galaxy, Gamora and Nebula were Thanos best assassins. So, it's an entire group of unicorns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T06:22:16-08:00","id":1526703,"title":"","content":"That's also the standard for superhero characters. Like, DC and Marvel are entire universes full of unique superpowered snowflakes. And it's not a genre created by millennials either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T15:41:39-08:00","id":1526779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526682#post1526682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah well, those may be Gen X writers, but they weren't writing for the smallest generation ever (at the time), they were writing for the Millennials. That was the target audience.<br /> <br /> Now, your social circle may be made of exclusively by &quot;depressed queers&quot; as you put it, but I assure you that this demographic represents a minority of the overall population. And people aren't robots fabricated in series. I from my part have met several happy and positive queers of my generation.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;white heteronormative males&quot;, as a &quot;white heteronormative male&quot; myself I don't particularly enjoy having my own traits - to which I have absolutely no fault of my own to possess, after all I didn't choose to be born with them - being so lightly throw away in such a derogatory fashion. I'm sure you don't like that kind of experience either so. There's no need to despise people based on their colour of skin, gender or sexual orientation, don't you agree? (Besides, J.K.R is not a male last time I checked)</div> </div> </div> </div>So first of all, it seems a little contradictory to try and defend with the claim that people &quot;aren't robots fabricated in a series&quot; when the argument you are trying to defend with that claim is one which lumps entire generations into boxes with collections of traits that you've decided to associate with them.<br /> <br /> Also, as another &quot;white heteronormative male,&quot; I understood that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28074_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28074\" data-vbnamecard=\"28074\">Doktor von Zwitter</a> was talking about white heteronormative males as protagonists in fiction, not the idea that the creators were any such thing. They were simply focusing on whether or not the creators were &quot;Millennials&quot; with &quot;Millennial&quot; traits or interests in that case; you were looking solely at the target audience, in contrast. It was a simple miscommunication. But more importantly, white het male protagonists no longer being treated as the default option is them (rightly) being removed from a pedestal, not thrown away. It's not about despising anyone, it's about fairness and representation.<br /> <br /> Like, I've avoided this thread until now on purpose, but your entire line of argument seems more like a bunch of Facebook memes than a genuine engagement with other &quot;Millennials&quot; as people. Seeing as how I know a bunch of people in my own age range, I can tell you that they run the frigging gamut, with as many defying the stereotypes you're tossing around as fitting into them.<br /> <br /> The thing that you really seem to be missing when you talk about stuff like Harry Potter and Guardians of the Galaxy is that you're talking about fiction written for <b>children</b>. Like, I know we used to terrify kids with stories about monsters that would gobble them up if they didn't do their chores or brush their teeth, but I feel like the transition away from that has been a good bit longer than the last 20 to 30 years. Like, I feel like a lot of your complaints would probably land pretty well on most Disney movies ever made. You know, the people who own Marvel.<br /> <br /> And why does Peter Quill get to be the gold-standard for the Millennial mindset anyways? I don't know if I can think of a single Millennial I know who looks at him and goes &quot;Yes, that is the dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the idea of certain people being special as an exclusively Millennial trait is kind of insane. Half the story of the Lord of the Rings is built around a guy being pretty much divinely mandated to be king. Not to mention an angel slumming as a wizard on their side. The fact that the dudes on the other side are just Average Joes who manage to pull it together and push through doesn't change that fact. Most of the stories that the current superhero trend is built on were written before Millennials were even born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T15:51:03-08:00","id":1526780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526700#post1526700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not due to him being immature. He may have a 80's cultural taste, but he behaves like a Millennial, not like a Gen X. Gen X are individualists. A Gen X media is like Highlander, where &quot;there can only be one&quot;. Millennials, despite the stereotype of being spoiled and immature (which sometimes is true but not always), are actually good at cooperating and working with others, and are usually optimistic. That's basically all that Guardians of the Galaxy is about, they learn to work together and to &quot;make the world (or galaxy in this case) a better place&quot;. Those are typical Millennial traits.<br /> <br /> He does have one Gen X trait thou, which is his nomadim. Gen Xers are more prone than others to not set roots in one place.<br /> <br /> Take in contrast for instance Back to the Future, where the protagonist is just a nobody common boy, who wins the day by being outright smarter than his opponents, and every mistakes he makes dooms the world to a utterly over the top cynical dystopian alternative future. So, he has to be THE BEST otherwise he's screwed. That's a very Gen X view of the world, as opposed to being the special &quot;Starlord&quot; who later on finds out to be a demigod. The rest of the Guardians are all special too mind you. They are all unique unicorns. Groot and the Raccoon are unique in the Galaxy, Gamora and Nebula were Thanos best assassins. So, it's an entire group of unicorns</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019re ignoring Gen Z in this discussion, as well as stereotyping both Gen X and Millennials unfairly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T18:58:38-08:00","id":1526789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_po