er":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T09:21:53-08:00","id":1526853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526789#post1526789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bOh damn, how did I miss this post? Are you for real right now?<br /> <br /> I literally said &quot;characters&quot;, referring to Harry Potter and Star Lord themselves, and you literally took it personally, which calls into question about what is even going on in your head right now.<br /> <br /> Last I checked, there aren't any laws being made against you currently. Sit down.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't any laws being made about blacks either, but if I had made the exactly same statement that you did but replacing it with &quot;blacks&quot;, I'm sure we would be having an entirely different discussion.<br /> <br /> But nice try at hiding your own bigotry and hatred pal. Unfortunately for you thou, I'm not the kind to just let it slide and remain quiet. Do not try to be condescending towards me and to tell me to shut up when you are directly and unapologetically attacking my very identity as a human being. Your bigotry will be exposed regardless of either or not you believe I should just shut up and accept it, no sir. Not on my watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T09:47:07-08:00","id":1526857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526779#post1526779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first of all, it seems a little contradictory to try and defend with the claim that people &quot;aren't robots fabricated in a series&quot; when the argument you are trying to defend with that claim is one which lumps entire generations into boxes with collections of traits that you've decided to associate with them.<br /> <br /> Also, as another &quot;white heteronormative male,&quot; I understood that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28074_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28074\" data-vbnamecard=\"28074\">Doktor von Zwitter</a> was talking about white heteronormative males as protagonists in fiction, not the idea that the creators were any such thing. They were simply focusing on whether or not the creators were &quot;Millennials&quot; with &quot;Millennial&quot; traits or interests in that case; you were looking solely at the target audience, in contrast. It was a simple miscommunication. But more importantly, white het male protagonists no longer being treated as the default option is them (rightly) being removed from a pedestal, not thrown away. It's not about despising anyone, it's about fairness and representation.<br /> <br /> Like, I've avoided this thread until now on purpose, but your entire line of argument seems more like a bunch of Facebook memes than a genuine engagement with other &quot;Millennials&quot; as people. Seeing as how I know a bunch of people in my own age range, I can tell you that they run the frigging gamut, with as many defying the stereotypes you're tossing around as fitting into them.<br /> <br /> The thing that you really seem to be missing when you talk about stuff like Harry Potter and Guardians of the Galaxy is that you're talking about fiction written for <b>children</b>. Like, I know we used to terrify kids with stories about monsters that would gobble them up if they didn't do their chores or brush their teeth, but I feel like the transition away from that has been a good bit longer than the last 20 to 30 years. Like, I feel like a lot of your complaints would probably land pretty well on most Disney movies ever made. You know, the people who own Marvel.<br /> <br /> And why does Peter Quill get to be the gold-standard for the Millennial mindset anyways? I don't know if I can think of a single Millennial I know who looks at him and goes &quot;Yes, that is the dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the idea of certain people being special as an exclusively Millennial trait is kind of insane. Half the story of the Lord of the Rings is built around a guy being pretty much divinely mandated to be king. Not to mention an angel slumming as a wizard on their side. The fact that the dudes on the other side are just Average Joes who manage to pull it together and push through doesn't change that fact. Most of the stories that the current superhero trend is built on were written before Millennials were even born.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Harry Potter was released when we Millennials were teens or children ourselves, so yeah, you just confirmed my point.<br /> <br /> Aragorn was NOT the main protagonist of Lord of the Rings; Frodo is. And Frodo was designed to be the quintessential average Joe; Frodo is the representation of the common soldiers fighting in the fields of battle, an experience that JRTolkien knew first hand, including losing many of his friends at the battle of Sonme, the bloodiest in history.<br /> <br /> And even considering Aragorn, he isn't &quot;special&quot; due to his blood. Gondor and Armor had plenty of kings before him. Aragorn developed a HUGE amount of skills over decades being a ranger, and he used those to guide and help others at the cost of his self sacrifice (people who haven't read the books don't know how Aragorn's history is a sad one about loss).<br /> <br /> Aragorn don't defeat the bad guy simply because he's the &quot;Chosen One&quot;. In fact, he doesn't defeat Sauron AT ALL - Frodo does. He just helps.<br /> <br /> About &quot;people not being robots&quot;, it's really tiresome to have to constantly explain the painfully obvious. And the reason why is because this smells more of intellectual dishonesty (aka &quot;win the argument at any cost, even outright lying or distorting words) rather than genuine ignorance.<br /> <br /> If I say that the medieval Mongols were &quot;aggressive conquerors&quot;, that means that MOST Mongols were favorable towards pillaging and genociding and enslaving and subjugating other people.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that 100,00% of all Mongols though that? I don't know, probably not. Maybe some monks didn't favor it. Does that make the generalization wrong, the fact that some exceptions exist? NO, YOU FOOL.<br /> <br /> If I say that &quot;Western people like freedom&quot;, that's a generalization. Does it mean that 100,00% of all westerners like freedom? Absolutely not, undoubtedly there are many who would want to live under tyranny. But those exceptions do NOT invalidate the rule.<br /> <br /> This is so painfully obvious that I shouldn't have to explain such a concept. Only a simpleton would even make such a point, and since I don't believe it to be your case, I can only infer that you are arguing in bad faith. And I don't argue with people who is intellectually dishonest, so goodbye.<br /> <br /> But you're probably the kind of person that would argue &quot;NoT aLL nAzIs&quot;... That is, if you wanted to be intellectually honest. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-15-2023, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T09:49:47-08:00","id":1526859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526780#post1526780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you\u2019re ignoring Gen Z in this discussion, as well as stereotyping both Gen X and Millennials unfairly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mention Gen Z because they were not relevant for the discussion so far. Gen Z's story is the Hunger Games. Gen Z are antisocial, being raised by the cynical Gen X. Hunger Games encapsulates perfectly their spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T10:20:17-08:00","id":1526862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526857#post1526857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harry Potter was released when we Millennials were teens or children ourselves, so yeah, you just confirmed my point.<br /> <br /> Aragorn was NOT the main protagonist of Lord of the Rings; Frodo is. And Frodo was designed to be the quintessential average Joe; Frodo is the representation of the common soldiers fighting in the fields of battle, an experience that JRTolkien knew first hand, including losing many of his friends at the battle of Sonme, the bloodiest in history.<br /> <br /> And even considering Aragorn, he isn't &quot;special&quot; due to his blood. Gondor and Armor had plenty of kings before him. Aragorn developed a HUGE amount of skills over decades being a ranger, and he used those to guide and help others at the cost of his self sacrifice (people who haven't read the books don't know how Aragorn's history is a sad one about loss).<br /> <br /> Aragorn don't defeat the bad guy simply because he's the &quot;Chosen One&quot;. In fact, he doesn't defeat Sauron AT ALL - Frodo does. He just helps.<br /> <br /> About &quot;people not being robots&quot;, it's really tiresome to have to constantly explain the painfully obvious. And the reason why is because this smells more of intellectual dishonesty (aka &quot;win the argument at any cost, even outright lying or distorting words) rather than genuine ignorance.<br /> <br /> If I say that the medieval Mongols were &quot;aggressive conquerors&quot;, that means that MOST Mongols were favorable towards pillaging and genociding and enslaving and subjugating other people.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that 100,00% of all Mongols though that? I don't know, probably not. Maybe some monks didn't favor it. Does that make the generalization wrong, the fact that some exceptions exist? NO, YOU FOOL.<br /> <br /> If I say that &quot;Western people like freedom&quot;, that's a generalization. Does it mean that 100,00% of all westerners like freedom? Absolutely not, undoubtedly there are many who would want to live under tyranny. But those exceptions do NOT invalidate the rule.<br /> <br /> This is so painfully obvious that I shouldn't have to explain such a concept. Only a simpleton would even make such a point, and since I don't believe it to be your case, I can only infer that you are arguing in bad faith. And I don't argue with people who is intellectually dishonest, so goodbye.<br /> <br /> But you're probably the kind of person that would argue &quot;NoT aLL nAzIs&quot;... That is, if you wanted to be intellectually honest. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to need you to clarify what &quot;point&quot; you think that I confirmed. I'm having a bit of a hard time following your rambling train of thought.<br /> <br /> So I think it should be pretty clear to anyone who has actually followed the story of the Lord of the Rings closely would understand that trying to simplistically insist &quot;Frodo's the protagonist, not Aragorn!&quot; misses a lot. Basically, from the end of the FotR onwards, the Lord of the Rings splits into (mostly) two stories. Each of those stories has it's own &quot;protagonist,&quot; each narrative centred around one of the characters. Frodo is one of them. Aragorn is the other. And both of their contributions to the ultimate destruction of the Ring are equally important. Frodo wasn't making it to Mount Doom with Sauron's legions camped out waiting for him. (Similar to how the Wheel of Time effectively has <b>three</b> protagonists. Sure, Rand al'Thor is probably the most important one, but you can go pretty much an entire book without him because there are entire stories happening without him being directly involved, and he never would have succeeded without everyone else.)<br /> <br /> Also, the argument that Aragorn isn't special is kind of ridiculous. Aragorn assembled the incredible skillset that he has because he's descended from a divinely-blessed hero-race; he's around his 80s or something during the time of LotR. He is pretty much the embodiment of the divine right of kings, with so much of his story centred around the idea that he and he ALONE is the only one who can reclaim the throne because of fantasy bloodright.<br /> <br /> (Also, I missed that little tidbit the first time, but I used to read the books once a year, so nice try acting like I just don't know the source material. It's been a while since I was a true Tolkien nerd, but I've done my homework.)<br /> <br /> The problem with your example is that the Mongols were an identifiable culture. Nazis are an identifiable ideology. You can identify those people by their voluntary association with certain beliefs or ideas, and frequently a willingness to adopt the cultural/ideological label in question. In contrast, generations are a post-hoc category made up and applied to people after the fact, and the concept is pretty frequently criticized for its arbitrariness. To the extent that there is science studying &quot;Millennials&quot; as a group, it generally doesn't back up the stereotypes you're tossing around either. Adam Conover did a talk about the concept of Millennials that was really good, and covers a lot of what I find frustrating about this.<br /> <br /> My calling you out on the &quot;robots&quot; comment is to call you out on the fact that you're trying to have it both ways without offering any reasonable justification that can comprehend for when it's ok to lump people into a stereotype like &quot;generations&quot; and when they must be treated as unique individuals beyond &quot;whenever I want to.&quot; It's not bad faith, it's just that you don't organize your ideas very well in my opinion, or you don't bother to provide adequate justification.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that you're clearly getting worked up and throwing around ad hominems doesn't help your case. I don't need to attack you as a person to call out the contradictions and shortcomings in your arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":".  Apparently I need to include credentials. 12-15-2023, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T11:18:02-08:00","id":1526865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526859#post1526859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mention Gen Z because they were not relevant for the discussion so far. Gen Z's story is the Hunger Games. Gen Z are antisocial, being raised by the cynical Gen X. Hunger Games encapsulates perfectly their spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Gen Z is very social (though mostly online) and into the power of cooperation and friendship. I\u2019m not a member of Gen Z, but I\u2019ve met enough of them to draw this conclusion (though again it\u2019s difficult to generalize about generations and individuals can definitely differ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-15-2023, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T11:28:53-08:00","id":1526866,"title":"","content":"I often think that when it comes to the various generations, the stereotypes are not so much a matter of what they are like but of who is most visible and who we've chosen to see as representative. Gen X as a generation isn't necessarily more cynical and rebellious, but the most visible parts were <i>or</i> the parts that were were made the representatives of that generation.<br /> <br /> Or in the case of baby boomers, the ones who remain in the spotlight to be representatives of that generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T12:08:15-08:00","id":1526867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526857#post1526857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harry Potter was released when we Millennials were teens or children ourselves, so yeah, you just confirmed my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes it a common experience among millennials and perhaps even a formative one. But that\u2019s not equivalent to WOD. If I\u2019m not mistaken, WOD was written by gen x young adults with gen x sensibilities for gen x teenagers and other gen xers their own age.<br /> <br /> Harry Potter skewed younger than that, at children who hadn\u2019t lacked the education to start challenging their inherited outlooks with new ideas. Years later, a lot of us are rather critical of it. Not just \u201cWhat were they thinking about \u2018Gypsies\u2019?\u201d, we\u2019re willing to write off the whole series. Because apart from those points that we might say \u201cdidn\u2019t age well\u201d, the essence of Harry Potter isn\u2019t as special as that of WoD, LotR etc (I suck literary criticism so everything is je ne said quoi in my words.)<br /> <br /> What culture for children demonstrates gen x cynicism? All I can think of is Daria, which was aired the same year as The Philosopher\u2019s Stone was published.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T12:33:19-08:00","id":1526868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526853#post1526853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There aren't any laws being made about blacks either, but if I had made the exactly same statement that you did but replacing it with &quot;blacks&quot;, I'm sure we would be having an entirely different discussion.<br /> <br /> But nice try at hiding your own bigotry and hatred pal. Unfortunately for you thou, I'm not the kind to just let it slide and remain quiet. Do not try to be condescending towards me and to tell me to shut up when you are directly and unapologetically attacking my very identity as a human being. Your bigotry will be exposed regardless of either or not you believe I should just shut up and accept it, no sir. Not on my watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are one of those people. No, Black people suffer other fucked up shit like getting gunned down for just existing. You, on the other hand, don't suffer any kind of oppression whatsoever. The equivalencies you draw are non-existent.<br /> <br /> You have, however, shown everyone here exactly what sort of person you are. Project much?<br /> <br /> And I'm not your &quot;pal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T13:28:02-08:00","id":1526873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526866#post1526866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often think that when it comes to the various generations, the stereotypes are not so much a matter of what they are like but of who is most visible and who we've chosen to see as representative. Gen X as a generation isn't necessarily more cynical and rebellious, but the most visible parts were <i>or</i> the parts that were were made the representatives of that generation.<br /> <br /> Or in the case of baby boomers, the ones who remain in the spotlight to be representatives of that generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely a fair point. The stereotype of a generation is often defined by it's most visible/attention-grabbing characteristics. Generations are often defined by the conflict between the people within them as much as conflicts with other generations. The visible revolutionaries of each generation are conflicting with the conformists among their peers, not just &quot;old folks.&quot; They are all a part of the story, and it makes talk about universal traits among generations difficult beyond the most obvious life-altering events, like the World Wars or the Great Depression. You can't really universalize about earlier generations without discussing the fundamental ways that racial discrimination would have drastically altered the experiences of non-white people in America from their white peers who are part of the same generation.<br /> <br /> Generation works as a broad strokes tool, but you shouldn't be using it as the foundation for making factual claims, in my opinion. You have to be tying your arguments to something more tangible, the actual history people have experienced. And yeah, that often involves a lot of convoluted nuance and nitpicking, but that's what's required to have a rational conversation about this sort of stuff, I think.<br /> <br /> Moving the conversation back towards Cynicism in the World of Darkness, it's also worth point out how the beginnings of WoD line up pretty closely with the &quot;Dark&quot;/&quot;Iron Age&quot; of Comic Books, another example of how grit and edginess were popular with a certain portion of the population at that time. And there was probably a fair bit of crossover between &quot;comic book geek&quot; and &quot;tabletop roleplaying geek.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T15:47:22-08:00","id":1526882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526868#post1526868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Black people suffer other fucked up shit like getting gunned down for just existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, there are still laws being passed to target black people. In Alabama the courts struck down a gerrymandered map (those maps are passed as laws) this year, because it was gerrymandered in a racist fashion... and then the Alabama legislature ignored the courts because they wanted to keep doing something that was declared legally racist against black people, and the courts had to draw a not-racist map themselves instead. We're not just cleaning up the centuries of mess left by all the racist laws in the US, we still have new ones to stamp down on too.<br /> <br /> You've got even more facts on your side.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> To the general concept on &quot;generations&quot; as a viable concept:<br /> <br /> Generations aren't about people. Not macro-trends, or individual visibility. Generations are about media consumption. There's a reason why the Western generation labels don't go past the Lost Generation. The Lost Generation was the generation that saw the the radio and telephone become a practical devices; they grew up in a world where instantaneous long distance non-line-of-sight communication wasn't a thing, and then it was a thing in their lifetime. The Greatest Generation grew up with the idea of telecommunication as a fact of life, but during its infancy. The Silent Generation was when in-home telecommunication became part of normal everyday life; they were effectively the &quot;radio&quot; generation. The Boomers were the television generation. Gen X is a combination of the portable media generation, and like the Lost Generation, the one on the cusp of the digital revolution in telecommunications. Millenials are the World Wide Web generation, where the Internet became part of daily life but was still shaped by various limitations even if those were solved faster than the early wireless generations did. And Gen Z is the Streaming generation where the Internet isn't just park of live, but media consumption is available on demand.<br /> <br /> Everything else about how we treat social generations as groups stems from this. For contemporaneous narratives largely driven by marketing firms trying to ply their trade now that their messages can get beamed into people's homes, to later stereotypes built around media consumption habits and the bias of what media stands the test of time, the underlying factor is how those broad groups got that media in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T16:42:29-08:00","id":1526886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote