yourself. Now do me that small courtesy and speak clearly, without twisting words. Because if by being &quot;one of these people&quot; means not being a hateful bigot like you, them I'm absolutely proud to be &quot;one of these people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Have a nice day, &quot;pal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T16:56:17-08:00","id":1526887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526873#post1526873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is definitely a fair point. The stereotype of a generation is often defined by it's most visible/attention-grabbing characteristics. Generations are often defined by the conflict between the people within them as much as conflicts with other generations. The visible revolutionaries of each generation are conflicting with the conformists among their peers, not just &quot;old folks.&quot; They are all a part of the story, and it makes talk about universal traits among generations difficult beyond the most obvious life-altering events, like the World Wars or the Great Depression. You can't really universalize about earlier generations without discussing the fundamental ways that racial discrimination would have drastically altered the experiences of non-white people in America from their white peers who are part of the same generation.<br /> <br /> Generation works as a broad strokes tool, but you shouldn't be using it as the foundation for making factual claims, in my opinion. You have to be tying your arguments to something more tangible, the actual history people have experienced. And yeah, that often involves a lot of convoluted nuance and nitpicking, but that's what's required to have a rational conversation about this sort of stuff, I think.<br /> <br /> Moving the conversation back towards Cynicism in the World of Darkness, it's also worth point out how the beginnings of WoD line up pretty closely with the &quot;Dark&quot;/&quot;Iron Age&quot; of Comic Books, another example of how grit and edginess were popular with a certain portion of the population at that time. And there was probably a fair bit of crossover between &quot;comic book geek&quot; and &quot;tabletop roleplaying geek.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are we saying that a temporal &quot;Zeitgeist&quot; is just a fantasy? The people of the 19th century didn't live in a Zeitgeist upon which they declared that &quot;God is Dead&quot;, and that science would solve all the mysteries and create an utopia? And that Zeitgeist didn't come crushing down after the two world wars, were all the wondrous creations of science were used for the most senseless and inhumane slaughtering in history, were the power of the machine that was supposed to end hunger and wars and diseases, was used for a bloody meat grinder without any purpose or meaning? Didn't the people of the late 19th century were Romantics in their worldviews, only for the Zeitgeist to turn into &quot;Realists&quot; from 20th century onwards?<br /> <br /> So, the chaotic Rome previous to Julius Caesar had the same Zeitgeist as the reactionary conservative Rome post Octavio Augustus? Are you telling me that society as a whole (not on an individual level) doesn't change its political &quot;overtone window&quot; with time at all, or that it is completely random or it is irrelevant or somewhat a fantasy that different times breed different ways of thinking?<br /> <br /> Wasn't the fascist movements a reactionary response towards the rise of communism?<br /> <br /> But wait, that's impossible since it is all just random right... The idea of a &quot;Zeitgeist&quot; is just pure fantasy, so it is impossible for something like Fascism to have existed. Or for Octavio Augustus conservative reforms of Rome... Or countless other examples. Perhaps the French Revolutionaries just thought they wanted egualite, liberte and fraternite. They actually just wanted to keep feudalism as it was, or perhaps it was just random... Probably 50/50 on the society. Yeah probably.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but that's an absurd proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T21:39:17-08:00","id":1526898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1525827-why-is-wod-so-cynical?p=1526886#post1526886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, we live in a word that has no